{"id": "EUVD-2026-93120", "enisaUuid": "3c3f16af-de11-3c6e-bd3c-e555f494aaa7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: wcn36xx: Fix potential use-after-free in TX ack timer teardown\n\nwcn36xx_dxe_deinit() tears down the TX ack timer with timer_delete(),\nwhich only dequeues the timer and does not wait for a callback that is\nalready executing; the preceding free_irq() calls synchronize the\ninterrupt handlers only. The callback, wcn36xx_dxe_tx_timer(), can\ntherefore be running past the teardown and use the wcn freed along\nwith the ieee80211_hw in wcn36xx_remove(): it takes wcn->dxe_lock,\nreads wcn->tx_ack_skb and passes wcn->hw to\nieee80211_tx_status_irqsafe().\n\nFix this by using timer_shutdown_sync(), which waits for a running\ncallback and also prevents the timer from being rearmed again. The\ntimer is set up again by wcn36xx_dxe_init() on the next start, so the\nstart/stop cycle is unaffected.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:32", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/15e59e377facc87ce82228279d88efaa89fdbca5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3edabc965bcce49cbb2ec1c2b91f8a555a8ec8bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2bddc5d088cf430ecd913020472f1def32a36a3d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0df0878e9110909cf0bec6080d72d36401a0c89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d9be5e75530772fc31637070d51e5717d6aeaa2a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98192", "GHSA-hrqp-97p2-7mmr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1d9e8127-8c08-31c9-96b1-61b7ec0e59a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fdf21cc3714939dd4327f3d664fe5863d15ccb31 <c0df0878e9110909cf0bec6080d72d36401a0c89"}, {"id": "5ce89046-4f67-366d-ab04-397fd64be919", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10"}, {"id": "64c77040-83d4-3e78-be7d-0b8d9c361af8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fdf21cc3714939dd4327f3d664fe5863d15ccb31 <d9be5e75530772fc31637070d51e5717d6aeaa2a"}, {"id": "93e69c96-6142-3cd6-ba0b-b3e5cfcc7252", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fdf21cc3714939dd4327f3d664fe5863d15ccb31 <3edabc965bcce49cbb2ec1c2b91f8a555a8ec8bd"}, {"id": "9990d2e4-02a2-32b6-aea0-c7119b69ca44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ac6105ab-2bee-315c-a562-27d69acab49c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "b239abfd-85ff-3244-9c39-8e4c230b6eac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "bad3b684-0606-3cac-b83c-511f48e76039", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "c77c4af1-86f9-3339-acdb-0bcb46cbc6d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "cc15deb8-4eda-3e2a-9f32-db06765d288b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fdf21cc3714939dd4327f3d664fe5863d15ccb31 <15e59e377facc87ce82228279d88efaa89fdbca5"}, {"id": "ce9c0cad-c1e4-3235-a92b-00929c583299", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "fdf21cc3714939dd4327f3d664fe5863d15ccb31 <2bddc5d088cf430ecd913020472f1def32a36a3d"}, {"id": "f2928fe3-3d04-32b2-8702-b461cc3f9dbe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8848ab26-7a24-3059-b5f9-6ec4c4303e50", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}